{"id":"summarize-noaa-hurricane-names","capability":"summarize","what":"外国机构的例行通报：分数走默认低分（进不了精选），但中文标题与摘要是人工写的。","match":{"urlIncludes":"noaa.gov","titleIncludes":"hurricane names"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.noaa.gov/weather/hurricane/2026-name-list","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"NOAA","title":"NOAA releases updated Atlantic hurricane name list","text":"NOAA announced the updated Atlantic hurricane name list, replacing four names retired after the previous season because of significant damage. Lists rotate on a six-year cycle and are maintained by the World Meteorological Organization."},"reply":{"titleZh":"NOAA 更新大西洋飓风季命名表，退役四个名字","summaryZh":"NOAA 公布新一期大西洋飓风季命名表，替换了上一季因造成重大损失而退役的四个名字；命名表按六年周期循环使用。此次调整不改变编号与预报流程。","bodyZh":""},"author":"tooling 示例（未核验）"}
{"id":"summarize-cl12","capability":"summarize","author":"地理编辑（气候与观测数据 beat）","what":"预估类研究按 T1 未达两倍门槛时的克制写法，保留“预估”标记","match":{"urlIncludes":"s43247-026-04075-w"},"guard":{"url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04075-w","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"Communications Earth & Environment","title":"Anthropogenic warming is projected to divert atmospheric rivers toward densely populated Asia","text":"Atmospheric rivers (ARs) are key drivers of extreme precipitation, and their future changes indicate major climate risks. Historical variations of ARs in Asia exhibited dynamic suppressions and thermodynamic enhancements under climate change, yet critical gaps remain in understanding the future impacts of these competing mechanisms. population exposure to AR-induced extreme precipitation is projected to increase across 58% of terrestrial AR-active zones, particularly in urban regions within northern China, India, and Bangladesh (+24–59%)"},"reply":{"titleZh":"预估大气河流转向亚洲，暴露人口或增24–59%","summaryZh":"《Communications Earth & Environment》一项用高分辨率全球气候模式集合做的预估显示，增暖下低纬度大气河流受动力抑制，而人口稠密的亚热带与中纬度以热力增强为主。作者预计 58% 的陆域大气河流活跃区人口暴露增加，中国北方、印度与孟加拉的城市地区增幅为 +24–59%；这是未来情景预估，不是已观测到的变化。","bodyZh":""}}
{"id":"summarize-rx18","capability":"summarize","author":"地理编辑（气候与观测数据 beat）","what":"目录页低分未入选，仍给人工中文标题与摘要","match":{"urlIncludes":"surface-air-temperature-maps"},"guard":{"url":"https://climate.copernicus.eu/surface-air-temperature-maps","sourceKind":"rss","sourceName":"Copernicus Climate Change Service","title":"Surface air temperature maps","text":"We produce surface air temperature maps as a data product, but you can also view the data directly. From April 2019 onward, the temperature summaries are based on ERA5. You can read more on the ' Climate Bulletin - About the data page '. Climate bulletin monthly maps index page."},"reply":{"titleZh":"哥白尼气温月报图件目录页","summaryZh":"Copernicus 地表气温月报的图件与数据目录页，按年份与月份列出各期条目，并说明 2019 年 4 月起的序列基于 ERA5、此前基于 ERA-Interim。本页不含本期新增数值与距平。","bodyZh":""}}
